{title: Visions of Iddo}
{subtitle: 2 Chronicles 9:29; 12:15; 13:22; Ezra 5:1; 6:14; Nehemiah 12:4–16}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] | [Cm7] |
| [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The acts of kings from begin[Bb/D]ning to end
[Cm7]Are written down for the peo[Ab]ple to learn
[Eb]In records found in the [Bb/D]ancient days
Where [Cm7]truth and history [Ab]gently lay
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
From Solomon’s throne to Re[Bb]hoboam’s reign
[Ab]The seer kept the sacred [Bb]chain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Visions of Iddo the [Bb]seer
Speaking concern[Cm7]ing Jer[Ab]oboam
His [Eb]words are the light that we [Bb]keep
Guiding the [Cm7]hearts in a [Bb]gentle [Ab]sweep
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Shemaiah’s notes and the ge[Bb/D]nealogies
[Cm7]Tell of the wars and the [Ab]histories
[Eb]Abijah’s ways and [Bb/D]his spoken words
Are recor[Cm7]ded in the [Ab]prophet’s chords
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
From the days of old to [Bb]the returning
A [Ab]spiritual line is for[Bb]ever turning
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Fm7] | [Ab] | [Eb] | [Bb/D] |
| [Fm7] | [Ab] | [Bbsus4] | [Bb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Zechariah son of [Bb/D]Iddo stands
In the [Cm7]name of the God of the [Ab]lands
[Eb]Haggai and Zechariah [Bb/D]prophesy
[Cm7]Building the temple with [Ab]faith and glee
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]The elders built and they [Bb/D]prospered on
Through the [Cm7]prophesy[Ab]ing until they were [Eb][Bb/D]done
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Cm7] | [Ab] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
